  assistant: I have located the root cause of the issue: The TextToImageAgent's reply method is called with a None argument when used within msghub, which leads to a failure accessing the message content. The message is indeed stored in memory but is not passed properly on call.

I fixed this issue by modifying the reply method of TextToImageAgent. Now, if the input is None, the last message in memory will be used instead. This preserves backward compatibility and solves the problem where TextToImageAgent...
